1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,603
Walking into a room and blanking on why you're there?

2
00:00:02,923 --> 00:00:09,330
A new Tufts University study points to three everyday foods behind it: ultra-processed snacks, processed meat, and sugary drinks.

3
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:20,282
That study tracked over 10,000 adults for eight years - people over 50 getting a fifth of their calories from ultra-processed snacks and frozen meals showed cognitive decline about 35% faster.

4
00:00:20,602 --> 00:00:22,619
Swap the chip bag for nuts or berries.

5
00:00:22,939 --> 00:00:35,497
Processed meat matters too - a 2025 study found eating it daily, even just two strips of bacon, raised dementia risk 13%, adding roughly 1.6 years of cognitive aging per additional daily serving.

6
00:00:35,817 --> 00:00:42,810
Try swapping in nuts, legumes, chicken, or fish instead - nuts and legumes alone were linked to a 20% lower risk.

7
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:52,906
Sugary drinks hit memory hardest - Boston University's Framingham Heart Study found drinking more than two a day matched memory scores 11 years older, plus a smaller hippocampus.

8
00:00:53,226 --> 00:00:57,259
Reach for sparkling water instead - same fizz, none of the sugar.
